faqs:
  - q: What counts as a production-ready AI system?
    a: Monitoring for latency, cost, drift, and output quality. A rollback path. An on-call rotation or handover. Without those, it is a demo.
  - q: Do you build on top of our existing data warehouse?
    a: Yes. Most LLM and forecasting pipelines pull from the warehouse you already have. We avoid adding stores unless the workload truly needs one.
  - q: What if the business case is unclear?
    a: We run a short scope phase first. If the ROI does not hold up, we say so and propose a smaller pilot. We would rather not start than ship something that gets shelved.
  - q: How do you handle hallucinations?
    a: Evaluation harnesses, retrieval quality work, prompt regression tests, and a guardrail layer. Where the domain needs it, we add human-in-the-loop review.
  - q: Can you run the system for us after launch?
    a: Yes. See /managed-services/mlops/ for the day-two shape.
